
 viewwebusage - Report WEB data file usage on the DSS Web Server.

 Queries the 'wusage' table in PostgreSQL database 'rdadb' and produces
 a usage view/report grouped and filtered by the options you choose.

 USAGE:
   viewwebusage [-C] ColumnNames [-O OrderColumnNames]
                <one or more condition options>
                [output and miscellaneous options]
                [> OutputFile] [| lp -d PrinterName]

 BASIC RULES:

   1. -C ColumnNames is required (see COLUMN OPTIONS below).
      The '-C' flag may be omitted if ColumnNames is the first argument.

   2. At least one condition option must be given:
        -a -c -d -D -e -E -f -F -i -I -k -l -m -M -N -o -q -S -t -T
        -v -V -y

   3. Negation: for any condition option except -a, prepend '!' between
      the flag and value to invert the filter, e.g. '-o ! DSS'.

   4. Wildcards: condition options that take strings (-c, -e, -f, -i, -k,
      -l, -o, -S, -t, -v) accept SQL wildcards '%' (any chars) and '_'
      (one char).

   5. By default the output is paginated with a header, footer, and
      column titles. Use -w for plain output (no header/totals).


 COLUMN OPTIONS:

   -C ColumnNames
        A string of one or more column letters listed below. The display
        order of columns matches their order in the string. At least one
        group column or summary column is required.

   -O OrderColumnNames
        Sort the output. Each letter must also appear in -C.
        UPPERCASE = ascending, lowercase = descending.

   Column letters:

     Group Columns:
       D* - DATE      - YYYY-MM-DD (e.g. 2004-04-25)
       E* - EMAIL     - user email address
       F* - FILENAME  - WEB file name accessed
       G* - PRODUCT   - product (top group) information
       I* - FIRSTNAME - user first name
       K* - REGION    - region name of the user
       L* - LASTNAME  - user last name
       M* - MONTH     - YYYY-MM (e.g. 2004-04)
       N* - COUNTRY   - country code of the user
       O* - ORGTYPE   - organization type (DSS, NCAR, UNIV, OTHER)
       P* - DSOWNER   - login name of the dataset-owning specialist
       Q* - QUARTER   - 1, 2, 3, or 4
       R* - DSTITLE   - dataset title
       T* - DATASET   - format dsnnn.n (e.g. d540001)
       V* - IPADDRESS - n.n.n.n
       W* - METHOD    - download method
       Y* - YEAR      - YYYY
       Z  - TIME      - time the file was read

       (*) = column may be displayed with zero usages when -z is used.

     Summary Columns:
       A - DSCOUNT    - number of datasets in the group
       B - MBYTEREAD  - data size (MB) read by the group
       C - #UNIQUSER  - number of unique users in the group
       H - #READ      - number of reads by the group
       J - #UNIQFILE  - number of unique files in the group
       U - #UNIQIP    - number of unique IP addresses in the group

     Index Column:
       X - INDEX      - 1-based row index (use as the first column)


 CONDITION OPTIONS:

   -a   All WEB file usages recorded since 2005-01-01.
   -A RowLimit                       Limit the number of rows returned.
   -c CountryCodes                   Users from these country codes.
   -d DateList                       Reads on the given dates (YYYY-MM-DD).
   -D StartDate [EndDate]            Reads between two dates.
   -e EMailList                      Reads by users with these emails.
   -E StartDate [EndDate]            Reads by users notified of dataset
                                     updates between these dates.
   -f FileNameList                   These WEB file names.
   -F MinFileName [MaxFileName]      WEB file names in this range.
   -h                                Pair with -e to include historical
                                     emails users registered with.
   -i FirstNameList                  Users with these first names.
   -I EmailIDList                    Reads by users for these email IDs.
   -j                                Include Group IDs in the PRODUCT column.
   -J                                Include Group Titles in the PRODUCT
                                     column.
   -k RegionNames                    Users from these regions.
   -l LastNameList                   Users with these last names.
   -m MonthList                      Reads in these months (YYYY-MM).
   -M DownloadMethodList             Reads via these download methods.
   -N MinReads [MaxReads]            Groups with read counts in this range.
   -o OrgTypes                       Users from these org types.
                                     Default: '-o ! DSS' (excludes DSS).
                                     Use '-o ALL' to include every type.
   -q QuarterList                    Reads in these quarters (1-4).
   -S SpecialistLoginNames           Specialists who own the datasets.
   -t DatasetList                    Reads of these datasets.
   -T MinDataset [MaxDataset]        Reads of datasets in this ID range,
                                     e.g. '-T d540000 d550009'.
   -v IPAddressList                  Reads from these IP addresses.
   -V MinIPAddress [MaxIPAddress]    Reads from this IP-address range.
   -y YearList                       Reads in these years (YYYY).


 OUTPUT AND MISCELLANEOUS OPTIONS:

   -H Title           Replace the default report title.
   -L Delimiter       Use Delimiter between columns instead of spaces.
   -U SizeUnit        Show sizes in unit: B, K, M, or G.
   -w                 Simple format: no header, no totals.
   -z                 Include zero usages for the specified fields.
   > OutputFile       Redirect output to a file.
   | lp -d Printer    Send output to the named printer (e.g. lj100).


 EXAMPLES:

   View annual WEB usage in 2005 with columns INDEX, EMAIL, ORGTYPE,
   #READ, MBYTEREAD; sort by ORGTYPE ascending and MBYTEREAD descending:

      viewwebusage XEOHB -y 2005 -O Ob

   Same, restricted to files matching 'Y%':

      viewwebusage XEOHB -y 2005 -f Y% -O Ob

   Same, excluding DSS users, and save to a file:

      viewwebusage XEOHB -y 2005 -f Y% -o ! DSS -O Ob > webusage.out
